.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt ZPOOL-STATUS-EXPORTER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zpool-status-exporter
.Nd Prometheus exporter for ZFS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -web.listen-address Ns = Ns Ar address
.Op Fl -web.config.file Ns = Ns Ar file
.Op Fl -web.systemd-socket
.Op Fl -web.telemetry-path Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -\&[no-\&]collector. Ns Ar name
.Op Fl -collect.interval Ns = Ns Ar duration
.Op Fl -collect.dataset-interval Ns = Ns Ar duration
.Op Fl -collect.smart-interval Ns = Ns Ar duration
.Op Fl -collect.timeout Ns = Ns Ar duration
.Op Fl -path. Ns Ar tool Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl -log.level Ns = Ns Ar level
.Op Fl -log.format Ns = Ns Ar format
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon is a Prometheus exporter for the Zettabyte File System (ZFS).
It serves metrics over Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) for a Prometheus server to scrape.
FreeBSD is the primary target platform.
Linux is supported on a best-effort basis.
.Pp
The exporter runs as root because Self-Monitoring, Analysis and Reporting Technology (SMART) queries need raw access to disk devices.
With the
.Cm smart
collector disabled, it can run as an unprivileged user.
.Pp
Each collector gathers data from the following sources.
Collectors run in the background at their own interval, and a scrape returns the most recent result.
.Bl -tag -width "datasets"
.It Cm pool
Pool and virtual device (vdev) state, capacity, errors, and scrub and resilver progress, from
.Ql zpool status -j
and
.Ql zpool list -j .
.It Cm iostat
Pool and vdev input and output (I/O) rates and latencies, from
.Ql zpool iostat -Hpvl -y Ar interval Li 1 .
.It Cm arc
Adaptive Replacement Cache (ARC) statistics, from
.Ql sysctl kstat.zfs.misc.arcstats
on FreeBSD and from
.Pa /proc/spl/kstat/zfs/arcstats
on Linux.
.It Cm kstat
Other ZFS kernel statistics (kstat) for the ZFS Intent Log (ZIL), dmu_tx, zfetch, abd, dnode, and vdev mirror, and per-dataset I/O counters.
.It Cm datasets
Dataset space usage, from
.Xr zfs 8
.Ql get .
.It Cm smart
SMART data, from
.Ql smartctl -j -x -n standby .
Disks in standby are not woken.
.El
.Pp
All metric names begin with
.Li zfs_ .
The README in the project repository lists every metric with its labels and meaning.
.Pp
The disk-to-device mapping uses
.Xr geom 8
and
.Xr glabel 8
on FreeBSD and
.Xr lsblk 8
on Linux.
.Sh OPTIONS
Options are parsed by kingpin and accept either
.Fl -option Ns = Ns Ar value
or
.Fl -option Ar value .
Every boolean
.Fl -collector. Ns Ar name
option also has a
.Fl -no-collector. Ns Ar name
form that disables the collector.
.Ss Web server
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -web.listen-address Ns = Ns Ar address
Address and port to listen on.
May be given more than once.
The default is
.Li :10058 .
.It Fl -web.config.file Ns = Ns Ar file
Path to an exporter-toolkit web configuration file that enables Transport Layer Security (TLS) and basic authentication.
The default is empty, which serves plain HTTP without authentication.
.It Fl -web.systemd-socket
Use systemd socket activation instead of a listen address.
Available on Linux only.
.It Fl -web.telemetry-path Ns = Ns Ar path
Path that serves metrics.
The default is
.Pa /metrics .
The health check is served at
.Pa /healthz .
.El
.Ss Collectors
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -collector.pool
Collect pool and vdev state.
Enabled by default.
.It Fl -collector.iostat
Collect pool and vdev I/O rates and latencies.
Enabled by default.
.It Fl -collector.arc
Collect ARC statistics.
Enabled by default.
.It Fl -collector.kstat
Collect other ZFS kernel statistics.
Enabled by default.
.It Fl -collector.datasets
Collect dataset space usage.
Enabled by default.
.It Fl -collector.smart
Collect SMART data.
Enabled by default.
.El
.Ss Intervals
Durations use the Go syntax, such as
.Li 500ms ,
.Li 10s ,
or
.Li 5m .
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -collect.interval Ns = Ns Ar duration
Collection interval of the pool, iostat, arc, and kstat collectors.
The default is
.Li 10s .
.It Fl -collect.dataset-interval Ns = Ns Ar duration
Collection interval of the datasets collector.
The default is
.Li 1m .
.It Fl -collect.smart-interval Ns = Ns Ar duration
Collection interval of the smart collector.
The default is
.Li 10m .
.It Fl -collect.timeout Ns = Ns Ar duration
Timeout for each external command.
The default is
.Li 30s .
.El
.Ss Tool paths
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -path.zpool Ns = Ns Ar path
The
.Xr zpool 8
command.
The default is
.Li zpool .
.It Fl -path.zfs Ns = Ns Ar path
The
.Xr zfs 8
command.
The default is
.Li zfs .
.It Fl -path.smartctl Ns = Ns Ar path
The
.Xr smartctl 8
command.
The default is
.Li smartctl .
.It Fl -path.sysctl Ns = Ns Ar path
The
.Xr sysctl 8
command.
The default is
.Li sysctl .
.It Fl -path.geom Ns = Ns Ar path
The
.Xr geom 8
command.
The default is
.Li geom .
.It Fl -path.glabel Ns = Ns Ar path
The
.Xr glabel 8
command.
The default is
.Li glabel .
.It Fl -path.lsblk Ns = Ns Ar path
The
.Xr lsblk 8
command.
The default is
.Li lsblk .
.It Fl -path.kstat Ns = Ns Ar path
Directory that holds the Linux ZFS kernel statistics.
The default is
.Pa /proc/spl/kstat/zfs .
.El
.Pp
A command name without a slash is looked up in the
.Ev PATH .
.Ss Logging and information
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -log.level Ns = Ns Ar level
Log verbosity: debug, info, warn, or error.
The default is
.Li info .
.It Fl -log.format Ns = Ns Ar format
Log format: logfmt or json.
The default is
.Li logfmt .
.It Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print version information and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev zpool_status_exporter_listen_address"
.It Ev PATH
Used to find the commands that the exporter runs.
The FreeBSD rc script adds
.Pa /sbin ,
.Pa /usr/sbin ,
.Pa /usr/local/sbin ,
and
.Pa /usr/local/bin .
.It Ev ZPOOL_STATUS_EXPORTER_ARGS
Linux only.
Command-line arguments that the systemd unit passes to the exporter, set in
.Pa /etc/sysconfig/zpool-status-exporter .
.El
.Ss rc.conf variables
The following variables are read from
.Xr rc.conf 5
by the rc script on FreeBSD.
.Bl -tag -width ".Va zpool_status_exporter_listen_address"
.It Va zpool_status_exporter_enable
Set to
.Dq YES
to start the exporter at boot.
The default is
.Dq NO .
.It Va zpool_status_exporter_listen_address
Address and port passed to
.Fl -web.listen-address .
The default is
.Dq :10058 .
.It Va zpool_status_exporter_args
Additional command-line arguments.
The default is empty.
.It Va zpool_status_exporter_user
User that runs the exporter.
The default is
.Dq root .
.El
.Pp
The script runs the exporter under
.Xr daemon 8 ,
which restarts it when it exits and sends its output to
.Xr syslogd 8
with the tag
.Dq zpool_status_exporter .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /usr/local/share/man/man8/zpool-status-exporter.8.gz" -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/zpool-status-exporter
Executable on FreeBSD.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/zpool_status_exporter
rc script on FreeBSD.
.It Pa /var/run/zpool_status_exporter.pid
Process identifier file of the exporter on FreeBSD.
.It Pa /var/run/zpool_status_exporter_supervisor.pid
Process identifier file of the
.Xr daemon 8
supervisor on FreeBSD.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/man/man8/zpool-status-exporter.8.gz
Manual page on FreeBSD.
.It Pa /usr/bin/zpool-status-exporter
Executable on Linux.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/zpool-status-exporter.service
systemd unit on Linux.
.It Pa /etc/sysconfig/zpool-status-exporter
Environment file of the systemd unit on Linux.
.It Pa /usr/share/man/man8/zpool-status-exporter.8.gz
Manual page on Linux.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Enable the exporter on FreeBSD:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysrc zpool_status_exporter_enable=YES
service zpool_status_exporter start
.Ed
.Pp
Listen on one address only, and disable the SMART collector, in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zpool_status_exporter_enable="YES"
zpool_status_exporter_listen_address="192.0.2.10:10058"
zpool_status_exporter_args="--no-collector.smart"
.Ed
.Pp
Enable the exporter on Linux:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
systemctl enable --now zpool-status-exporter
.Ed
.Pp
Scrape the exporter from Prometheus:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
scrape_configs:
  - job_name: zpool-status-exporter
    scrape_interval: 15s
    static_configs:
      - targets: ["storage.example.net:10058"]
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr geom 8 ,
.Xr glabel 8 ,
.Xr smartctl 8 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr zpool 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility was written to export ZFS pool, cache, dataset, and disk health metrics from FreeBSD to Prometheus.
